1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,032
My tongue felt heavy because every single word you speak turns into solid stone inside your pocket.

2
00:00:07,332 --> 00:00:16,188
Leo stumbled down the narrow alley, clutching his canvas jacket as jagged boulders strained the worn seams.

3
00:00:16,488 --> 00:00:24,648
He had argued too much at work today, leaving his coat pockets crammed with jagged, painful conversation fragments.

4
00:00:24,948 --> 00:00:32,700
Most people learned to whisper early, trading meaningful glances instead of risking the crushing weight of gossip.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:41,232
Leo reached his apartment door, desperate to drop his heavy burden and finally enjoy a moment of absolute quiet.

6
00:00:41,532 --> 00:00:49,956
Inside, he emptied his pockets onto the steel scale, watching the jagged gray rocks pile up alarmingly high.

7
00:00:50,256 --> 00:00:59,448
The scale blinked red, showing ten kilograms. But Leo had stayed completely silent during his entire shift today.

8
00:00:59,748 --> 00:01:06,900
He picked up a heavy stone and smashed it open, expecting to find his own spoken complaints inside.

9
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:15,120
Instead, tiny whispered insults from his neighbors spilled out, proving he had been carrying everyone else's judgment.

10
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:21,996
If our unspoken thoughts weigh us down this much, whose voice is really breaking your back right now?
